        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-17T16:45:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggest initializing the deep sleep expire time so that deep sleep won\u0027t happen for the first ~15 sec after the system boots.  That gives a window of time to connect with JTAG or disable deep sleep at the console before the first deep sleep could occur.\n\nFor example, just set console_in_use\u003d1 and console_expire_time \u003d (now + 15 sec).\n\n(Yes, normally we boot the AP right at system start, but there are cases where we don\u0027t - for example, if the system is booted with power+refresh+downarrow to debug a problem with chipset startup.)",
      "revId": "577769eb8a9632961a9a475c02a6920b3872d51a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "def0a8a0_ae25f7ba",
        "filename": "chip/lm4/clock.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 295,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-17T16:45:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "...or if the UART transmit buffer isn\u0027t empty (tx_buf_head !\u003d tx_buf_tail in uart_buffering.c)\n\nIf we pause UART output with soft flow control (Ctrl+S), we don\u0027t want to deep sleep, or else we\u0027ll eat the Ctrl+Q character which would resume UART output.",
      "revId": "577769eb8a9632961a9a475c02a6920b3872d51a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
